---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

/**
 * WCAG 2.1 AA is a TARGET here, never a conformance CLAIM.
 *
 * The FTC fined accessiBe $1M for repeating a vendor's compliance claim. An
 * unqualified "this site is accessible" is a representation that can be tested
 * and found false. No overlay widget, ever — they are the thing that got fined.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Accessibility"
  description="What we aim for on accessibility, what we know isn't there yet, and how to tell us about a barrier."
  path="/accessibility"
  updated="16 July 2026"
  summary="What we aim for, what we know is missing, and how to tell us when something blocks you."
>
  <h2 id="aim">What we aim for</h2>
  <p>
    We build against <strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> as a target. That means
    the things it actually asks for: text you can read, contrast you can see,
    everything reachable with a keyboard, sensible headings, real labels on form
    fields, and motion that respects your system settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We are not claiming conformance.</strong> "Target" and "conformant"
    are different words and we are using the accurate one. Claiming a standard we
    have not been independently audited against would be a statement we cannot
    stand behind — and telling you the truth costs us nothing.
  </p>

  <h2 id="done">What's in place</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Semantic HTML, so screen readers get real structure rather than a pile of divs.</li>
    <li>A skip link to jump straight to content.</li>
    <li>Visible focus indicators on everything focusable.</li>
    <li>Body text meeting AA contrast against its background.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Animation respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>.</strong>
      The product demonstrations on this site stop animating entirely and show a
      finished, static state instead — they don't just slow down.
    </li>
    <li>Text that reflows and stays readable when zoomed or on a narrow screen.</li>
    <li>Nothing conveyed by colour alone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="gaps">What we know isn't there yet</h2>
  <p>Being specific is more useful than a reassuring paragraph:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <span class="wip">In progress</span> The site has not been independently
      audited, and has not been tested end-to-end with every major screen reader.
      Our confidence comes from how it is built, not from a test report.
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="wip">In progress</span> The animated product demonstrations
      are visual by nature. They carry a reduced-motion alternative and none of
      them contains information you can't get from the surrounding text — but
      they are not a substitute for a described walkthrough, and we know it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="wip">In progress</span> The product itself, at
      app.igrowfast.com, is a dense operational tool held to the same target but
      not yet at the same level as this site. It is being worked on.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="overlay">No accessibility overlay</h2>
  <p>
    We don't use an overlay widget — the kind that bolts a floating accessibility
    button onto a site and promises instant compliance. They frequently make
    things worse for the people they claim to help, and they interfere with the
    assistive technology you already have configured. We would rather fix the
    underlying page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tell">Tell us</h2>
  <p>
    If something on this site or in the product blocks you, we want to know — and
    we would rather hear about it than have you work around it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:contact@igrowfast.com">contact@igrowfast.com</a> with
    what you were trying to do, the page, and what got in the way. If you tell us
    which assistive technology and browser you use, that helps us reproduce it.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will acknowledge within a few days and tell you honestly whether it's a
    quick fix or a longer one. If you need information from this site in another
    format in the meantime, ask and we will send it to you directly.
  </p>
</Legal>

<style>
  code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--line-soft);
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
